.TH "REPROCTL\-DOCTOR" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-doctor \- diagnose the development environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl\f[R] [\f[B]\(enjson\f[R]] \f[B]doctor\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a series of health checks against the local development environment
and reports pass, warn, or fail for each item.
.PP
With the global \f[B]\(enjson\f[R] flag, outputs a JSON object with an
\f[B]items\f[R] array where each item has \f[B]name\f[R],
\f[B]status\f[R] (ok, warn, or fail), and optional \f[B]expected\f[R],
\f[B]actual\f[R], and \f[B]message\f[R] fields.
.PP
The following checks are performed:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]brew\f[R] \(em Homebrew is installed and functional.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]direnv\f[R] \(em direnv is installed and hooked into the shell.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]kind\f[R] \(em kind CLI is available.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]pandoc\f[R] \(em pandoc document converter is available (used for
manpage generation).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]postgresql\(at17\f[R] \(em PostgreSQL 17 client tools are on PATH.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]proto\f[R] \(em proto toolchain manager is installed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]node\f[R] \(em Node.js is available at the expected version.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]pnpm\f[R] \(em pnpm package manager is available.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]moon\f[R] \(em moon build tool is available.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]tilt\f[R] \(em Tilt is installed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]helm\f[R] \(em Helm is installed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]ctlptl\f[R] \(em ctlptl is installed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]docker\f[R] \(em Docker daemon is running.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]cluster\f[R] \(em The kind cluster exists and is reachable.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]registry\f[R] \(em The local container registry is running.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]pnpm install\f[R] \(em Node modules are up to date.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B].envrc\f[R] \(em The .envrc file is trusted by direnv.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
All checks pass.
Warnings are acceptable.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
One or more checks failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl doctor
Run all health checks.
.TP
reproctl \(enjson doctor
Output health checks as JSON.
